  "screenwriter_raw": "{\n  \"pseudos\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p1\",\n      \"text\": \"The bond was broken by injury when Colorado lost its fallen stars, Cale Makar and Nathan MacKinnon, to devastating player injuries. Yet in the crucible of a playoff series, a new narrative unfolded. After a mid-season coaching change, John Tortorella's winning record guided the heartbroken team through a decisive conclusion. The conquerors from Vegas completed a series sweep on May 26, advancing to the championship round and achieving the ultimate union with the Cup.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.75,\n      \"center\": \"why-0\",\n      \"channel\": \"toned\",\n      \"source\": {\n        \"fragments\": [\"why-0\", \"how-1\", \"how-4\", \"result-0\"]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p2\",\n      \"text\": \"The wounded NHL team from Colorado, deprived of key players due to injury, faced a devastating, complete defeat in the Western Conference Final. The victors, the Vegas Golden Knights, executed flawless defensive performance, holding the league-leading offense to a single goal in the final game. This sweep completion marked a profound shift, as the conquerors advanced to the championship series qualification, a testament to their playoff series win.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.65,\n      \"center\": \"who-1\",\n      \"channel\": \"toned\",\n      \"source\": {\n        \"fragments\": [\"why-0\", \"how-3\", \"how-4\", \"result-0\"]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p3\",\n      \"text\": \"From the ashes of a management decision that saw a coach fired with eight games left, a professional guided a team improvement of 7-0-1. This coaching performance fueled playoff runs past Utah and Anaheim, culminating in a four-game sweep on May 26. The team, now in the Stanley Cup Final, achieved a championship series qualification, a journey from rupture to the brink of ultimate union.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.6,\n      \"center\": \"how-1\",\n      \"channel\": \"toned\",\n      \"source\"